==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{m|is|leggja á||to put on}}, from {{m|is|leggja||to put, to lay}} and {{m|is|á||on}} and {{m|is|minnið||the memory}} the definite article accusative singular of {{m|is|minni||memory}}.

===Noun===
{{is-verb-weak|lagði|lagt|11=á minnið}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[keep]] in [[mind]], to [[memorise]], to [[study]], to [[learn]]
#: ''Allir þurfa að '''leggja''' reglurnar '''á minnið'''.''
#:: Everybody needs to '''memorise''' the rules.

====Usage notes====
* The thing or object which is being ''memorised'' or ''kept in mind'' is used between {{m|is|leggja}} and {{term||á minnið|on memory}} in the accusative form:
*: ''Við þurfum að '''leggja''' alla bókina '''á minnið''' fyrir prófið!''
*:: We need to '''memorise''' the whole book for the test.

